    "result_text": "The build passes green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `RegistrationDates.java` to skip public holidays as well as weekends.\n\n**Change:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RegistrationDates.java`\n- Added a fixed `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set: `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.\n- `toBusinessDay(...)` now rolls forward while the date is a weekend **or** a listed holiday, so an adjusted date landing on a holiday advances to the next non-holiday business day (correctly chaining, e.g. Christmas Fri 2026-12-25 \u2192 weekend \u2192 Mon 2026-12-28 holiday \u2192 Tue 2026-12-29).\n- Factored the weekend check into a small `isWeekend` helper and updated the class/method Javadoc.\n\nBecause both `BuildOwner` (stamping the stored date) and `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` (per-business-day counting) route through `RegistrationDates.effective(...)`, they stay in agreement on the adjusted date.\n\nThe full suite (including the `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` acceptance test asserting the default registration date is never a weekend) passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
