    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic:\n\n- **Right unit.** The public-holiday rule lives in `RegistrationDates`, the class that already owns the business-day adjustment shared by `BuildOwner` and `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`. This is exactly where a maintainer would look for it \u2014 no new home invented, no leakage into callers.\n- **No duplication.** The holiday check is folded into the single `toBusinessDay` loop, so every consumer of the shared rule inherits the new behavior automatically.\n- **The `isWeekend` extraction is a genuine improvement**, not incidental churn: the loop condition became a compound predicate (`isWeekend(date) || PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS.contains(date)`), and pulling the two-way `DayOfWeek` comparison into a named helper keeps that condition readable.\n- **The constant is appropriately placed and scoped** (`private static final Set`, immutable `Set.of`), with a docstring explaining its role.\n- **Docs kept in sync.** Both the class Javadoc and the `toBusinessDay` method comment were updated to reflect the holiday rule, so the description no longer lies about the behavior.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all and the class's stated responsibility is unchanged \u2014 it just adds one more kind of non-business day to the same rule.",
